    "institutions_today": [],
    "paragraph": "\"Road-Closure Stress Testing of Essential-Service Accessibility in Yemen\" developed a national network stress test using OpenStreetMap road data and WorldPop population grids to model access to markets, health facilities, and fuel stations for 41.18 million people across 8,460 cells. \"Effects of urban green spaces on visiting population of railway station areas\" analyzed the relationship between urban green spaces and the staying population within railway station catchment areas. \"Geometric and topological analysis of convergence and divergence in urban water pipeline and road networks across regions\" compared the geometric and topological structures of water pipeline and road networks across Kigali, Kisumu, La Rochelle, and Vancouver.",
